## Event-Driven Patterns

```php
<?php

// Event
namespace App\Events;

use App\Models\Market;
use Illuminate\Foundation\Events\Dispatchable;
use Illuminate\Queue\SerializesModels;

class MarketCreated
{
    use Dispatchable, SerializesModels;

    public function __construct(
        public Market $market
    ) {}
}

// Listener
namespace App\Listeners;

use App\Events\MarketCreated;
use App\Jobs\SendMarketCreatedNotification;

class NotifySubscribersOfNewMarket
{
    public function handle(MarketCreated $event): void
    {
        SendMarketCreatedNotification::dispatch($event->market);
    }
}

// Register in EventServiceProvider
protected $listen = [
    MarketCreated::class => [
        NotifySubscribersOfNewMarket::class,
        UpdateMarketCache::class,
        LogMarketCreation::class,
    ],
];

// Dispatch event
event(new MarketCreated($market));
```

**Remember**: Laravel patterns enable scalable, maintainable PHP applications. Leverage Laravel's built-in features and conventions for clean, testable code.
